        "question": "Explain the terms (a) flocculation, (b) pH, (c) acid dissociation constant (Ka), (d) conjugate pair.",
        "marks": 18,
        "model": "Flocculation: The process where colloidal particles aggregate into larger particles/flocs that settle out more readily due to reduced electrostatic repulsion between particles.\n\npH: A measure of hydrogen ion (H⁺) concentration in solution, defined as pH = –log[H⁺], where [H⁺] is the concentration of hydrogen ions in mol dm⁻³.\n\nAcid dissociation constant (Ka): The equilibrium constant for the dissociation of a weak acid; it measures the extent to which a weak acid ionises in aqueous solution. Larger Ka indicates stronger acid.\n\nConjugate pair: Two species differing by one proton (H⁺); if one is an acid, the other is its conjugate base, or if one is a base, the other is its conjugate acid.",
