        "question": "Which of the two compounds, A or C, would you expect to be more soluble in water?\nGive a reason for your answer.",
        "marks": 12,
        "model": "Compound C (ethanol, CH₃CH₂OH) is more soluble in water. Ethanol contains a hydroxyl (-OH) group capable of hydrogen bonding with water molecules. The O-H bond is highly polar, and the oxygen lone pairs accept hydrogen bonds from water. This extensive hydrogen bonding network makes ethanol miscible with water in all proportions. Compound A (ethyl bromide) is nonpolar and cannot form hydrogen bonds with water; it is only sparingly soluble, dissolving minimally through van der Waals interactions.",
