        "model": "Compound B (ethene, CH₂=CH₂) can be polymerised. Under heat and pressure with a catalyst (e.g. Ziegler-Natta catalyst), the C=C double bonds open and link together through addition polymerisation, forming polyethene (polythene). The polymer chain consists of repeating -CH₂-CH₂- units.\n\nUse: Polyethene is used extensively in plastic film for packaging, bags, and cling film due to its flexibility, water resistance, and low cost. It is also used in rigid applications such as milk bottles and containers.",
