        "model": "Anti-bumping granules (glass or pumice stone) provide nucleation sites for smooth boiling. They prevent bumping/violent eruption of liquid by allowing even bubble formation throughout the liquid. This ensures controlled heating, prevents loss of reaction mixture through splashing, and maintains safe reaction conditions during reflux.",
