        "marks": 6,
        "model": "The solution was orange or orange-yellow. Sodium dichromate(VI) in acidic conditions (sulfuric acid present) produces this characteristic orange colour due to the dichromate ion (Cr₂O₇²⁻) in solution.",
        "diagram": "",
