        "question": "What colour was produced as the ethanol reacted with the sodium dichromate(VI)?",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "The colour changed from orange to green. As ethanol oxidises the dichromate(VI), the orange dichromate ion (Cr₂O₇²⁻) is reduced to the green chromium(III) ion (Cr³⁺). This colour change is the visual indicator of the oxidation-reduction reaction occurring.",
        "diagram": "",
