        "question": "Why was it important to reflux the reaction mixture?",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "Refluxing ensures complete oxidation of ethanol to ethanal (acetaldehyde). The prolonged heating drives the reaction to completion by constantly recycling unreacted ethanol and dichromate back into the reaction vessel. Reflux prevents loss of volatile ethanol and maximises product yield.",
