        "question": "What term is used to describe the type of flask shown in the diagram?",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "Volumetric flask (or graduated flask / measuring flask / standard flask). This is a flask with a narrow neck and a graduation mark on it, used to prepare standard solutions of exact, known concentration. The mark indicates the volume at which the solution should be made up to, ensuring accuracy in concentration.",
        "diagram": "",
        "model_source": "ai-h1"
