        "marks": 7,
        "model": "Le Châtelier's principle states: when a system at equilibrium is subjected to a stress (change in temperature, pressure, or concentration), the system shifts in a direction that opposes/counteracts that stress, re-establishing equilibrium. The equilibrium position moves to reduce the effect of the applied stress, either forward or backward depending on the nature of the disturbance.",
