        "label": "a(i)",
        "question": "The following names are associated with the development of our knowledge of the elements and atomic structure: Boyle, Curie, Dalton, Mendeleev, Rutherford. Who was the Co. Waterford-born scientist who gave us an important gas law and is described as 'the father of modern chemistry'?",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "Robert Boyle, born in Lismore, County Waterford (1627–1691), is described as 'the father of modern chemistry'. He established Boyle's Law, which states that for a fixed mass of gas at constant temperature, pressure is inversely proportional to volume (P ∝ 1/V). This fundamental relationship between gas pressure and volume became a cornerstone of gas theory and experimental chemistry.",
        "diagram": "",
