        "marks": 12,
        "model": "A conical flask contains hydrochloric acid. A gas syringe (or graduated tube inverted over water) is connected via rubber tubing to the flask. A thermometer can monitor temperature. The apparatus measures hydrogen gas collected over time. A diagram should show the flask sealed except for the delivery tube, the syringe graduated in cm³, and the connection secured. The setup allows continuous measurement of gas volume as magnesium reacts with acid.",
