        "model": "Plot volume of H₂ (y-axis, in cm³, 0–60) against time (x-axis, in seconds, 0–600). The curve shows rapid initial increase (steep gradient) as reaction rate is fastest when acid concentration is highest. The curve gradually flattens (gradient decreases) as acid concentration falls and fewer magnesium particles remain. The curve levels off (horizontal) when all magnesium is consumed and no more hydrogen evolves. Final volume plateau indicates reaction completion. The shape demonstrates inverse relationship between reactant concentration and time.",
