        "question": "The combustion of methane is described by the following balanced equation.\nCH₄(g) + 2O₂(g) → CO₂(g) + 2H₂O(l)     ΔH = −890.4 kJ mol⁻¹\nThe standard heats of formation of carbon dioxide and water are −394 and −286 kJ mol⁻¹ respectively.\nCalculate the heat of formation of methane.",
        "marks": 12,
