        "question": "Define the rate of a chemical reaction.",
        "marks": 5,
        "model": "The rate of a chemical reaction is the change in concentration of a reactant or product per unit time. It can be expressed as the decrease in concentration of a reactant (mol dm⁻³ s⁻¹) or the increase in concentration of a product (mol dm⁻³ s⁻¹) over a measured time interval.",
