        "question": "Explain why increasing the temperature has a significant effect on the rate of a reaction.",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "Increasing temperature increases the average kinetic energy of reactant molecules, causing them to move faster and collide more frequently and with greater energy. More collisions exceed the activation energy threshold, so a greater proportion of collisions are productive. Both increased collision frequency and increased proportion of effective collisions cause the rate to increase significantly.",
