        "question": "Use your knowledge of intermolecular forces to explain why methane has a very low boiling point (b.p. = –164 °C).\nThe relative molecular mass of methane is only slightly lower than that of water but the boiling point of water is much higher (b.p. = 100 °C). Suggest a reason for this.",
